273
00:13:47,530 --> 00:13:49,740
I helped you sneak around for six months.

274
00:13:49,910 --> 00:13:51,410
I looked like an idiot.

275
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:53,410
And I was humiliated.

276
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:55,290
And I only made $200.

277
00:13:57,330 --> 00:13:59,870
We didn't give you any money.

278
00:14:03,090 --> 00:14:04,880
You don't think I know that?

279
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:12,550
I can't decide if it goes better by the new chair...

280
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:13,760
the Sahara desk...

281
00:14:13,930 --> 00:14:16,180
or the Parker console table.

282
00:14:16,350 --> 00:14:18,770
I didn't know there was a Pottery Barn up here.

283
00:14:20,270 --> 00:14:22,520
I know, I went a little crazy.

284
00:14:20,270 --> 00:14:22,520
A little?

285
00:14:22,690 --> 00:14:25,570
Your place looks like page 72 of the catalog.

286
00:14:26,900 --> 00:14:28,280
Look at that!

287
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:32,570
The ornamental birdcage! Large.

288
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:32,570
Ha, ha.

289
00:14:35,370 --> 00:14:38,500
Oh, Ross? Be careful. That is very old.

290
00:14:38,660 --> 00:14:42,960
Colonial bird merchants used to bring their birds to market in that.

291
00:14:44,210 --> 00:14:45,500
Fascinating.

292
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:51,340
Another amazing find! Wow.

293
00:14:51,930 --> 00:14:54,970
I bet this has a great story too.

294
00:14:51,930 --> 00:14:54,970
It does.

295
00:14:55,140 --> 00:15:00,140
It is a room-separating apparatus from Colonial times.

296
00:15:00,730 --> 00:15:04,610
Huh, a lot of this stuff is from the Colonial times.

297
00:15:04,770 --> 00:15:07,820
What are some other time periods, Rachel?

298
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:11,820
Well, there's yore.

299
00:15:13,910 --> 00:15:17,870
Ahem, and, uh, you know, yesteryear.

300
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:22,790
Rachel has such a good eye for this stuff.

301
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:25,420
Ross, if you ever decide to redecorate...

302
00:15:25,590 --> 00:15:28,050
and I think you should...

303
00:15:28,210 --> 00:15:29,960
you should ask Rachel to help.

304
00:15:30,130 --> 00:15:31,670
Aw, he doesn't need my help.

305
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:35,140
I think he's ready to get rid of the... What'd you call it?

306
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:37,640
The, uh, "cheap knockoffs and dinosaur junk"?

307
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:44,270
Really?

308
00:15:45,310 --> 00:15:49,530
You know, since you have such a great sense of what I need...

309
00:15:49,690 --> 00:15:51,570
Uh, here's 60 bucks.

310
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:55,700
Why don't you take Phoebe down to that Colonial, uh, flea market...

311
00:15:55,870 --> 00:15:57,410
and get me some stuff?

312
00:16:02,290 --> 00:16:04,580
I don't think Phoebe wants to come.

313
00:16:04,750 --> 00:16:06,580
I do want to.

314
00:16:04,750 --> 00:16:06,580
She does want to.

315
00:16:06,750 --> 00:16:08,250
She does want to.

316
00:16:06,750 --> 00:16:08,250
Yeah!

317
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:18,260
I guess the flea market was just better last time.

318
00:16:18,430 --> 00:16:21,350
Well, at least I got these sheets for Ross.

319
00:16:22,730 --> 00:16:25,400
Ugh, look at this. Pottery Barn.

320
00:16:25,560 --> 00:16:29,110
Ugh, yeah, you know what? Don't look at it.

321
00:16:29,270 --> 00:16:31,780
Seriously, don't look at it.

322
00:16:29,270 --> 00:16:31,780
Look!

323
00:16:31,940 --> 00:16:34,150
There's the table they stole from us.

324
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:36,280
Oh, those bastards! Let's go.

325
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:42,450
That fan kind of looks like ours, and the birdcage, and...

326
00:16:42,830 --> 00:16:45,790
Wait a second, this is our exact living room!

327
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:48,130
No, it's not.

328
00:16:48,290 --> 00:16:50,630
Come on, ours is totally different.

329
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:54,590
I mean, we don't have the... We don't have that lamp.

330
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:59,760
And that screen is on the other side.

331
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:03,930
Oh, my God. This is where you got all our stuff.

332
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:07,100
Pottery Barn! Oh, my God!

333
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:07,100
No. No.

334
00:17:07,270 --> 00:17:09,730
Okay, I did, all right? I'm sorry.

335
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:13,990
I wanted this stuff and I know how you feel about Pottery Barn.

336
00:17:14,150 --> 00:17:17,070
Come on, don't be mad.

337
00:17:14,150 --> 00:17:17,070
No, but I am mad.

338
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:20,320
Because this stuff is what's wrong with the world...

339
00:17:20,490 --> 00:17:22,870
and it's in my living room...

340
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:27,000
and all I can think about is how I don't have that lamp!

341
00:17:28,210 --> 00:17:30,130
Well, then, honey, buy the lamp.

342
00:17:30,290 --> 00:17:32,630
We have that 60 bucks from Ross.

343
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:36,970
I can't! I can't!

344
00:17:37,470 --> 00:17:39,090
Unless...

345
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:43,100
Are you saying you'd move out if I didn't buy that lamp?

346
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,350
No, I'm not gonna move out!

347
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:49,480
But are you saying that you would move out if I didn't buy that lamp?

348
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:54,280
Yes! I would so move out.

349
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:54,280
Then I don't have a choice.

350
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:57,820
I have to buy that lamp!

351
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:57,820
That's right.

352
00:17:58,530 --> 00:18:00,820
But at least the apothecary table's real.

353
00:18:06,370 --> 00:18:09,920
This was great. Didn't everybody have a great time?

354
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:12,750
I did. I really did. And I've got to say...

355
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:16,460
I'm sorry if I was weird after the last time we went out.

356
00:18:16,630 --> 00:18:18,380
I guess I was just nervous.

357
00:18:18,550 --> 00:18:21,430
That's understandable.

358
00:18:18,550 --> 00:18:21,430
Don't worry about it.

359
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:22,850
So we can go out again?

360
00:18:23,010 --> 00:18:24,640
Absolutely.

361
00:18:23,010 --> 00:18:24,640
Well, good.

362
00:18:24,810 --> 00:18:27,060
Okay, well, good night.

363
00:18:24,810 --> 00:18:27,060
Good night.

364
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:33,270
See, huh?

365
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:34,690
Wasn't that fun?

366
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:36,780
We have got to move.

367
00:18:37,530 --> 00:18:38,990
What?

368
00:18:39,150 --> 00:18:40,490
I knew it!

369
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:44,700
You're not so quiet yourself, missy!

370
00:18:46,620 --> 00:18:49,580
I'm blah? The only thing more boring than modern dance...

371
00:18:49,750 --> 00:18:51,120
is you talking about it.

372
00:18:51,290 --> 00:18:52,750
Oh, Chandler...

373
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:54,960
I just lost myself in the movement."

374
00:18:58,170 --> 00:19:00,340
You know, I know you're talking...

375
00:19:00,510 --> 00:19:03,340
but all I hear is blah-blah-blah-blah-blah.

376
00:19:03,510 --> 00:19:06,890
All right, you and me! Let's go, right now!

377
00:19:07,060 --> 00:19:08,390
All right, enough!

378
00:19:09,230 --> 00:19:12,600
Enough! You two, go home. I gotta talk to Janine.

379
00:19:12,770 --> 00:19:15,230
I really think you could take her.

380
00:19:15,730 --> 00:19:17,980
You better hope I don't see you in the hallway!

381
00:19:23,410 --> 00:19:25,120
All right. Uh...

382
00:19:25,280 --> 00:19:27,990
Look, we got a little bit of a problem here.

383
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:30,620
You can't my treat my friends that way.

384
00:19:30,790 --> 00:19:35,380
They said stuff to me too.

385
00:19:30,790 --> 00:19:35,380
I know, I'll talk to them about it.

386
00:19:35,540 --> 00:19:37,250
They mean so much to me.

387
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:39,710
They're like my family, you know?

388
00:19:39,880 --> 00:19:43,050
If you guys are gonna be fighting all the time...

389
00:19:44,430 --> 00:19:48,310
I don't think we can be together. It just can't work, okay?

390
00:19:48,470 --> 00:19:49,640
It can't.

391
00:19:49,810 --> 00:19:51,600
I'm very upset.

392
00:19:53,230 --> 00:19:54,810
Okay.

393
00:19:54,980 --> 00:19:57,270
Would it help if I apologized?

394
00:19:57,480 --> 00:19:59,150
Yeah.

395
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:01,110
That'd be very helpful.

396
00:20:06,070 --> 00:20:08,780
What did I tell you about the hall?

397
00:20:10,870 --> 00:20:13,870
I was coming over to apologize for my behavior.

398
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:18,090
I'd really like it if we could be friends.

399
00:20:20,670 --> 00:20:24,930
Well, I know that would make Joey happy, so...

400
00:20:25,090 --> 00:20:27,220
I would like that too.

401
00:20:28,350 --> 00:20:30,890
Great.

402
00:20:28,350 --> 00:20:30,890
Now, come on.

403
00:20:33,980 --> 00:20:36,350
I'm glad we worked it out.

404
00:20:33,980 --> 00:20:36,350
Me too.

405
00:20:36,520 --> 00:20:38,480
I'll see you.

406
00:20:36,520 --> 00:20:38,480
Bye.

407
00:20:38,650 --> 00:20:41,820
Or I'll hear you.

408
00:20:38,650 --> 00:20:41,820
That's it, big girl!

409
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:45,490
Wait!

410
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:51,240
You'd better run!

411
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:54,120
Did you hear that?

412
00:20:55,290 --> 00:20:57,960
What am I gonna do?

413
00:20:55,290 --> 00:20:57,960
I'm sorry, man.

414
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:01,840
Want to go watch?

415
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:01,840
Yeah!

416
00:21:10,470 --> 00:21:11,510
Hey.

417
00:21:10,470 --> 00:21:11,510
Hey.

418
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:14,390
How you doing?

419
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:14,390
So, uh, did she move out?

420
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:16,390
Pretty much.

421
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:18,940
I can't believe you just broke up with her.

422
00:21:19,110 --> 00:21:21,190
When it's not right, you know it.

423
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:24,610
You okay?

424
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:24,610
I'll be all right.

425
00:21:25,860 --> 00:21:28,950
You know what'd cheer you up?

426
00:21:25,860 --> 00:21:28,950
What?

427
00:21:29,160 --> 00:21:33,080
I'm giving this lecture on erosion theories tomorrow night.

428
00:21:35,410 --> 00:21:37,160
I think you should come.

429
00:21:44,050 --> 00:21:46,300
You're right, that did cheer me up.

